This aircraft is derived from the "swan_k1_hwing" simulation model in ArduPilot's SITL_Models
(Gazebo/models/swan_k1_hwing), a model of the HEQ Swan K-1 HWing by Brandon MacDougall,
Andrew Tridgell and Rhys Mainwaring. It carries that model's geometry, mass, motor cant and
control layout; the fuselage and motor meshes are the source model's own, converted to glTF
and recoloured after the manufacturer's photographs. The propeller meshes are the Iris
propellers that model ships with.

SITL_Models distributes its Gazebo models as the ROS package "ardupilot_sitl_models" under
the GNU General Public License v3.0; see LICENSE in this folder for its text.

  https://github.com/ArduPilot/SITL_Models

The PX4 airframe file (px4_quadtailsitter) follows PX4-Autopilot's 4018_gz_quadtailsitter,
and the aerodynamic coefficients are the ones both that project's "quadtailsitter" Gazebo
model and the ArduPilot model carry. PX4-Autopilot is distributed under the BSD 3-Clause
License.

  https://github.com/PX4/PX4-Autopilot

The propeller thrust and power tables are taken from the UIUC Propeller Data Site
(Brandt, Deters, Ananda, Dantsker and Selig), APC 9x6E wind-tunnel measurements.

  https://m-selig.ae.illinois.edu/props/propDB.html
